[[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Use the radio removal tools\nsupplied.</p><p>1. Fit both tools into the slots on the front of the radio and push\nin until the mechanism holding the radio in place clicks open.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005050.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>1. Pull out the radio using the tools.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005051.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>1. Disconnect electrical connections (1a), (1b), (1c).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1a</p></td><td><p>Radio</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024588\">P20A</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Radio</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024590\">P20B</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1c</p></td><td><p>Radio</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024598\">P20C</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Disconnect the aerial connection.</p><p>3. Recover the radio set.</p><p>4. Release the tools and take out.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005052.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the radio set  is\nundamaged.</p><p>Connect the electrical connections and\nthe aerial lead.</p><p>Fit the radio into its compartment, taking\ncare not to compress the electrical wires.</p><p>Push the radio fully home until it locks\nin place.</p><p>Check the radio is working properly.</p>"]]